60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option A creates income but adds administrative burden.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,Option B is fair but ignores the daily reality of rain and access.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option C is chaotic. The frame trial showed it’s hard to use.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Option A funds maintenance. The ward park proves demand.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A is the only one that doesn’t collapse under weight.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, but the neighbourly block failed with charges.","{""words"":8,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,The residents said they’d rather pay than be equal. That supports A.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"If we do A, we need to automate billing to save the treasurer.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,We can’t automate easily. But the income covers the cost.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Toshio,,I can take the billing if it’s simple. But it must be simple.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I vote for A. It’s the only sustainable model.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I vote for A. People want to pay for certainty.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for A. It solves the morning shoving match.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,I vote for A. It balances the books.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I vote for A. It’s the only viable option.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
